# Git hooks must keep LF endings on every platform.
#
# ⚠ A `#!/bin/sh` script checked out with CRLF fails as "bad interpreter: No
# such file or directory" — the shell reads the trailing CR as part of the
# interpreter path. Windows clones default to CRLF on checkout, so without this
# the pre-commit hook would silently stop running for anyone on Windows: the
# worst failure mode for a guard, since it looks exactly like "no violations".
.githooks/** text eol=lf
